export default "Burning, urgency, peeing often, and bladder pressure can show up on their own. They can also show up near sex, near your period, or over and over.\n\nThis page is one tracker for all of it. It does not diagnose a UTI, cystitis, pregnancy, or any other cause. It helps you bring clear notes and good questions to a clinician.\n\nIt is not medical advice.\n\n## Call-out symptoms\n\nContact a clinician promptly if any of these fit.\n\n- [ ] Fever\n- [ ] Back or side pain\n- [ ] Nausea or vomiting\n- [ ] Blood in urine\n- [ ] Pregnancy or possible pregnancy\n- [ ] Symptoms feel severe\n- [ ] Symptoms are getting worse\n\nIf you feel very sick, seek urgent care.\n\nMayo Clinic says back or side pain, high fever, chills, nausea, and vomiting can happen when the kidneys are affected.\n\n## One-page visit sheet\n\nFill this out first, before a visit or portal message.\n\n| Question | Your note |\n|---|---|\n| Main symptom | |\n| Date it started | |\n| Burning when peeing | |\n| Strong urge to pee | |\n| Peeing often, with little urine | |\n| Lower belly pressure | |\n| Cloudy, bloody, or strong-smelling urine | |\n| Fever, chills, back pain, or side pain | |\n| Nausea or vomiting | |\n| Pregnancy or possible pregnancy | |\n| Sex timing, if you want to share it | |\n| Period timing, if relevant | |\n| Number of episodes like this in the past year | |\n| Main question for the clinician | |\n\nUse plain words. \"It burns when I pee\" is enough.\n\n## Daily symptom log\n\nUse one row per day. This works for a single episode, a period-timed pattern, or a recurring one.\n\n| Date | Cycle day | Period day | Urgency | How often you peed | Burning 0 to 10 | Pelvic pressure | Fever | Back or side pain | Blood in urine | Notes |\n|---|---:|---|---|---|---:|---|---|---|---|---|\n| | | | none, mild, strong | usual, more, a lot | | none, mild, strong | yes, no | yes, no | yes, no, not sure | |\n| | | | | | | | | | | |\n| | | | | | | | | | | |\n| | | | | | | | | | | |\n| | | | | | | | | | | |\n\nWrite what changed your day. \"Had to pee every hour\" helps. So does \"left work early.\"\n\n## Context that may matter\n\nOnly share what is needed for care.\n\n| Context | Your note |\n|---|---|\n| Symptoms near sex, if you want to share | |\n| Symptoms near period timing | |\n| New birth control or spermicide use | |\n| Perimenopause or menopause context | |\n| Diabetes or blood sugar concerns | |\n| Kidney stone history | |\n| Trouble emptying bladder | |\n| Pregnancy or possible pregnancy | |\n| Recent catheter or procedure | |\n\nSex timing and period timing can be clues in the visit story. They do not mean sex or your period caused your symptoms.\n\n## Recurrent episode timeline\n\nIf this keeps coming back, write one row for each episode you remember.\n\n| Date symptoms started | Main symptoms | Urine test done? | Culture done? | Medicine used | Did symptoms return? |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| | | yes / no / not sure | yes / no / not sure | | yes / no / not sure |\n| | | | | | |\n| | | | | | |\n| | | | | | |\n\nRough dates are okay. Office on Women's Health and Mayo Clinic say recurrent UTIs can mean two UTIs in six months or three in a year. Ask your clinician how your history fits.\n\n## Test records to gather\n\nBring portal screenshots or lab names if you have them.\n\n| Record | Date | Result, if known | Question |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Urine analysis | | | |\n| Urine culture | | | |\n| Pregnancy test, if relevant | | | |\n| STI testing, if relevant | | | |\n| Imaging, if done | | | |\n| Scope exam, if done | | | |\n\nAsk what each result means. Also ask what it does not rule out.\n\n## What not to assume\n\nDo not assume:\n\n- A period means urinary symptoms are normal.\n- A symptom near sex or ovulation has a clear cause.\n- A past UTI means this is the same thing.\n- A log can replace a urine test.\n- An app can tell you what treatment you need.\n\nThe goal is clearer notes, not self-diagnosis.\n\n## Questions to ask\n\nPick the questions that fit your situation.\n\n- Do my symptoms need a urine test today?\n- Do I need a urine culture?\n- Do my records fit recurrent UTI?\n- Could another cause fit my symptoms, such as cystitis, pregnancy, or a pelvic floor issue?\n- Should pregnancy change what we check?\n- What symptoms mean I should call sooner?\n- Do you need my full history, or is this summary enough?\n- Should I see gynecology, primary care, or urology?\n\nDo not use this page to choose antibiotics or change medicine. Ask your clinician what care fits you.\n\n## Short visit script\n\n> \"I have had urinary symptoms ________ times since ________. My main symptoms are ________. I have test results from ________. I want to know what needs testing and what follow-up fits.\"\n\nStart with the pattern. Then show the table.\n\n## One-page visit summary\n\nFill this in before you call or go in.\n\n| Summary item | Your note |\n|---|---|\n| Symptoms started | |\n| Worst burning score | |\n| Worst urgency score | |\n| Peeing often | |\n| Fever, back pain, nausea, or vomiting | |\n| Blood in urine | |\n| Pregnancy concern | |\n| Number of past episodes | |\n| Main question | |\n\n## Privacy note\n\nBladder notes can include sex timing, pregnancy worry, urine culture results, medicine, and location clues. Share the smallest useful record.\n\nAsk:\n\n- Do you need my full app history?\n- Is this summary enough?\n- Will these notes go in my chart?\n- Can I leave out private notes not tied to care?\n\nFloriva can keep dates and notes on your device. Paper works too. No app can promise full privacy. You still choose what to type, export, screenshot, print, or share.\n\nFor privacy help, read the [UTI and bladder data privacy checklist](/resources/privacy-in-practice/protect-your-symptom-and-condition-data). For visit prep, read [Floriva for gynecologist prep](/app-guides/floriva-for-gynecologist-prep).\n\n## Floriva note\n\nFloriva can keep short symptom and cycle notes on your device. It does not diagnose a UTI or any other condition. A clinician can review your pattern and decide what testing or care fits.";
